      },
      "narration": "I want to tell you about a specific moment that happens inside organizations all the time. A CFO walks into a board meeting and presents a churn rate. The number is on the slide. It looks precise. It has a decimal. Everyone in the room accepts it. And it is wrong. Not wrong because someone made a calculation error. Wrong because the AI that produced it queried the wrong table. In this lesson we are going to watch that happen step by step, inside this database, so you can see exactly how it occurs and exactly what it would take to prevent it.",
      "transition": "new_concept",
      "clears": [],
      "phases": []
    },
